1634
00:10:14,180 --> 00:10:18,110
This time he's with the Lord Theodore
and Royal Captain of the Guard Sieg,

1635
00:10:18,110 --> 00:10:21,390
then he'll be in competition with Count Hayden.

1636
00:10:21,670 --> 00:10:29,860
<i>Count Haydenâ€¦ I believe he's the one who runs Edea,
which borders our neighboring country Maldura.</i>

1637
00:10:30,320 --> 00:10:36,370
Lady Anna, how has your father,
Count Hayden, been doing recently?

1638
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,250
I think he's the same as always.

1639
00:10:44,550 --> 00:10:48,700
Oh? But hasn't it been hectic
in the Edea Domain since last year?

1640
00:10:48,700 --> 00:10:52,630
I've heard that a major trading company
has ventured into the Surian weave business.

1641
00:10:53,090 --> 00:10:59,150
Right now the Surian weave is extremely popular
even at the royal court, and I simply must find some as well.

1642
00:10:59,150 --> 00:11:03,020
Due to the special techniques used,
it isn't very easy to acquire.

1643
00:11:03,380 --> 00:11:10,570
Lady Elianna, you were the catalyst in reviving the Surian weaveâ€¦
Is there anything you can do to help us?

1644
00:11:10,570 --> 00:11:14,400
Well, I'm not involved in the production of it.

1645
00:11:14,690 --> 00:11:18,530
Why did you take such a sudden interest
in the long-dead Surian weave?

1646
00:11:18,950 --> 00:11:24,080
I became interested in it last year after I read
an ancient description from a continental merchant.

1647
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:28,040
Then, I got one made for me through a connection.

1648
00:11:28,040 --> 00:11:29,320
Wowâ€¦

1649
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:34,470
I hear there's a line of both nobles and merchants
asking for your hand in marriage, Lady Anna.

1650
00:11:34,470 --> 00:11:36,300
While I am grateful for that,

1651
00:11:36,660 --> 00:11:39,800
I have no intention of marrying anyone at the present.

1652
00:11:41,310 --> 00:11:43,130
No need to be so stiff.

1653
00:11:43,130 --> 00:11:44,700
None at all.

1654
00:11:44,700 --> 00:11:48,730
Lady Elianna, do you have connections
in other countries as well?

1655
00:11:49,050 --> 00:11:55,490
No. Since I had no connections in Maldura,
it was made using the yarn of Sauslind.

1656
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:57,740
Naturally.

1657
00:11:57,740 --> 00:12:00,490
If it were something made
from the raw material of Maldura,

1658
00:12:00,490 --> 00:12:02,490
I wouldn't even want to put my arm through the sleeves.

1659
00:12:02,490 --> 00:12:07,490
Indeed! Things from a savage country like that
are no doubt inferior goods.

1660
00:12:07,490 --> 00:12:08,620
No, they aren't.

1661
00:12:10,450 --> 00:12:13,750
The description was also from continental merchants
from a long time ago, but

1662
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:18,970
most recently, the "moonlight fabric"
mentioned in Mr. Gene Tucker's "Lovers of the Moon" series

1663
00:12:18,970 --> 00:12:23,260
may have been woven from Malduran materialsâ€¦

1664
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:26,060
You mean to say it actually existed?

1665
00:12:26,060 --> 00:12:30,370
Ah, well, I haven't taken time to look it up properly, butâ€¦

1666
00:12:30,370 --> 00:12:35,480
There's an account in the regional history of Edea territories
of what Lady Elianna was talking about.

1667
00:12:35,730 --> 00:12:42,740
Back then, the fabrics that came in from Maldura
were said to glimmer in the moonlight.

1668
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:50,750
How beautiful. Anything woven from that thread
becomes something even more exquisite.

1669
00:12:50,990 --> 00:12:52,610
Yes, it must be.

1670
00:12:52,610 --> 00:12:55,170
I'd love to see it just once.

1671
00:12:57,400 --> 00:12:58,430
What's the matter?

1672
00:12:58,430 --> 00:12:59,460
Are you alright?

1673
00:12:59,460 --> 00:13:01,620
Huh? I wonder what's happened?

1674
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:10,390
One young lady unaccustomed to horses was thrown off.

1675
00:13:10,390 --> 00:13:13,020
Oh dear, was she injured?

1676
00:13:13,020 --> 00:13:14,650
Seems she's hurt her leg.

1677
00:13:15,990 --> 00:13:17,540
Eli, big sister!

1678
00:13:17,540 --> 00:13:18,400
Lilia.

1679
00:13:19,400 --> 00:13:22,530
That person is entering the gentlemen's area on purpose!

1680
00:13:22,530 --> 00:13:24,160
Who is?

1681
00:13:24,160 --> 00:13:25,450
Lady Sofia!

1682
00:13:25,710 --> 00:13:29,460
What's more, she's asking Lord Theodore for help!

1683
00:13:30,180 --> 00:13:31,460
She wouldn't...

1684
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,220
Lady Elianna.

1685
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:45,720
I will be the one to make you
the Princess of Eidel this year in place of Chris.

1686
00:13:54,340 --> 00:13:55,810
<i>Lord Theodore?</i>

1687
00:13:58,570 --> 00:14:01,890
Eli, you must never act alone while you're here.

1688
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:19,160
Lady Elianna, may I have this dance?

1689
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:19,710
Yes.

1690
00:14:20,890 --> 00:14:22,810
Please save the next for me.

1691
00:14:22,810 --> 00:14:23,220
Okay.

1692
00:14:24,030 --> 00:14:25,010
Then one for me.

1693
00:14:25,010 --> 00:14:25,950
And me.

1694
00:14:25,950 --> 00:14:26,970
Y-Yes...

1695
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:32,230
<i>I am exhausted.</i>

1696
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,900
May I have this dance?

1697
00:14:34,900 --> 00:14:35,600
Okay!

1698
00:14:37,060 --> 00:14:38,610
Lord Theodore!

1699
00:14:40,570 --> 00:14:45,140
While it is admirable and heartwarming
to see you working so hard on behalf of Chris,

1700
00:14:45,140 --> 00:14:47,030
there's no need to feel so obligated.

1701
00:14:47,030 --> 00:14:48,120
But...

1702
00:14:49,010 --> 00:14:51,620
Well, you are who you are, and

1703
00:14:54,270 --> 00:14:57,750
Eli, that dress suits you perfectly.

1704
00:14:58,330 --> 00:15:02,260
The shades make you look as enchanting as a wine fairy,
enough to intoxicate me.

1705
00:15:04,610 --> 00:15:07,890
That dress suits you perfectly.

1706
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:11,890
Thank you, Lord Theodore.

1707
00:15:13,060 --> 00:15:16,070
Lady Lilia, please take care of Lady Elianna.

1708
00:15:16,070 --> 00:15:18,310
Yes, I've got her.

1709
00:15:18,310 --> 00:15:19,770
Take a little break.

1710
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:23,440
Oh, Miss Lilia.

1711
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:25,150
Here comes trouble...

1712
00:15:26,170 --> 00:15:30,410
Good evening, Miss Caroline, Miss Sofia, Miss Cecily.

1713
00:15:31,700 --> 00:15:34,390
How do you do, Miss Elianna?

1714
00:15:34,390 --> 00:15:36,290
It's a pleasure to meet you.

1715
00:15:37,040 --> 00:15:39,790
Miss Elianna, you sure love to dance, don't you?

1716
00:15:40,260 --> 00:15:41,670
Huh?

1717
00:15:41,670 --> 00:15:47,680
I nearly mistook you for a noblewoman
desperately trying to hunt down a marriage partner.

1718
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:49,760
Oh my, Cecily!

1719
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:55,430
You two, Lady Elianna currently holds the title
of fiancÃ©e of His Highness,

1720
00:15:55,430 --> 00:15:58,190
so of course she has no problem finding dance partners.

1721
00:15:58,190 --> 00:16:02,040
In that case, perhaps she should be more careful?

1722
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:07,630
Indeed, hard to believe the fiancÃ©e of His Highness
the Crown Prince would be such an uninhibited lady...

1723
00:16:07,630 --> 00:16:12,870
I can't believe there are people who can't differentiate
between being social and being immodest.

1724
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:18,250
Lady Sofia, how is your leg?

1725
00:16:18,690 --> 00:16:22,170
Eh? It's perfectly fine, thank you.

1726
00:16:22,170 --> 00:16:28,010
It may best to take it easy, there are some who say that
sprains can become chronic conditions.

1727
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:33,890
Some people say cooling it with horse meat
is more effective than using a poultice.

1728
00:16:34,130 --> 00:16:35,640
Horse meat?

1729
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:39,930
Yes, cooling the injury with raw horse meat.

1730
00:16:39,930 --> 00:16:47,150
It's folk medicine introduced from the Pasig Region,
but the efficacy is medically recognized.

1731
00:16:47,380 --> 00:16:51,990
The oil extracted from the fat of the horse,
called "equus oil," works well on burns,

1732
00:16:51,990 --> 00:16:54,990
and it's also good at clearing up a woman's skin.

1733
00:16:54,990 --> 00:16:58,120
Fresh horse fat is cut into small pieces,
and in a steam heating oven...

1734
00:16:58,120 --> 00:16:59,540
E-Excuse me...

1735
00:16:59,880 --> 00:17:01,500
I'm not feeling very...

1736
00:17:01,500 --> 00:17:02,420
Neither am I!

1737
00:17:02,420 --> 00:17:04,540
A-Are you okay?

1738
00:17:10,680 --> 00:17:12,610
The young lady of Marques Bernstein.

1739
00:17:13,890 --> 00:17:18,680
My name is Lowe Hayden,
and I am the lord of the Edea frontier territory.

1740
00:17:19,060 --> 00:17:22,150
I pray you will forgive me
for my ill-mannered introduction.

1741
00:17:23,110 --> 00:17:26,080
It's an honor to meet you.

1742
00:17:26,080 --> 00:17:30,150
I had hoped I would be able
to meet you at least once, to relay my gratitude.

1743
00:17:30,670 --> 00:17:31,780
Gratitude?

1744
00:17:33,360 --> 00:17:38,910
Thanks to you, Edea is buzzing
with a vibrancy rarely seen in recent years,

1745
00:17:38,910 --> 00:17:40,500
and you have my thanks for this.

1746
00:17:41,250 --> 00:17:43,380
There's no need to thank me.

1747
00:17:43,380 --> 00:17:48,510
I was surprised that someone living in the royal capitol
would turn their attention to those residing in the borderlands.

1748
00:17:49,160 --> 00:17:52,420
Though impudent, I thought of your activities very warmly.

1749
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:55,010
However,

1750
00:17:56,660 --> 00:18:01,270
I soon realized that I was sorely mistaken.

1751
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:09,030
The support sent to Maldura last year
that resulted in curbing it's military was splendid work.

1752
00:18:11,770 --> 00:18:15,740
I'm concerned the price of wheat will decline sharply
since we had such a plentiful harvest this year.

1753
00:18:15,740 --> 00:18:20,290
We're discussing counter measures
as a bargaining tool for the south.

1754
00:18:20,290 --> 00:18:21,290
Excuse me.

1755
00:18:21,290 --> 00:18:23,540
What is it, Elianna?

1756
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:29,550
I think it would be better if the government
bought up as much as possible as reserves.

1757
00:18:30,260 --> 00:18:31,260
Why?

1758
00:18:31,590 --> 00:18:37,510
The other day, I found a memo of
the old manager in the library.

1759
00:18:38,010 --> 00:18:41,400
In it I saw in the year that Sauslind had a good harvest,

1760
00:18:41,400 --> 00:18:45,190
other countries suffered damage
from a cold spell and drought,

1761
00:18:45,190 --> 00:18:49,480
and the year of the cold spell damage especially put
Maldura's internal affairs in disarray,

1762
00:18:49,480 --> 00:18:51,530
and there was also an invasion...

1763
00:18:52,430 --> 00:18:59,560
So based on the statistics I asked the weather officials
to confirm the weather conditions for this year,

1764
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:02,250
and in the northwestern region including Maldura,

1765
00:19:02,250 --> 00:19:05,870
there was a huge possiblity that
there would be cold spell damage.

1766
00:19:06,170 --> 00:19:13,380
If so, Maldura should contact the territories that
are likely to be attacked and take countermeasures.

1767
00:19:13,890 --> 00:19:16,500
When there's a threat of military attack to other countries,

1768
00:19:16,500 --> 00:19:20,970
do you feel safer just strengthening
your own country's defenses?

1769
00:19:20,970 --> 00:19:21,600
What?

1770
00:19:22,340 --> 00:19:28,610
Every time I read history books I thought it was strange.
Why doesn't war cease to exist?

1771
00:19:30,270 --> 00:19:36,220
It isn't about being able to put up a fight,
it's about nipping war in the bud before it can happen.

1772
00:19:36,220 --> 00:19:39,740
Isn't that truly the most important thing?

1773
00:19:40,880 --> 00:19:43,120
I agree that would be ideal, but...

1774
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:47,250
do you think that logic would make sense to
a country who boasts of their military power?

1775
00:19:48,410 --> 00:19:49,880
I don't.

1776
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:56,260
But why must we react to meet
the standards of the others?

1777
00:19:56,690 --> 00:20:00,340
We should have our own way of doing things.

1778
00:20:03,060 --> 00:20:08,470
If we have a plan before we get involved in war,
then we should employ those means.

1779
00:20:09,980 --> 00:20:16,520
Since we avoided war with Maldura,
this year's war budget has been significantly reduced.

1780
00:20:16,520 --> 00:20:18,410
Elianna, how would you use the funds?

1781
00:20:19,300 --> 00:20:24,790
I think it should be applied to renovating
the medical technology in the Krug Region.

1782
00:20:25,570 --> 00:20:30,630
However, have you ever thought about
how the people of Edea felt when they learned of this?

1783
00:20:32,170 --> 00:20:40,390
The people take pride in the fact that they always
defended their homeland from the dangers of war.

1784
00:20:40,770 --> 00:20:45,150
They don't like war, and I recognize that as well...

1785
00:20:45,150 --> 00:20:49,350
but a statement from your position
has the power to move the nation.

1786
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:54,550
You understanding that can only be taken
as the idealism of a dreamy young lady

1787
00:20:54,550 --> 00:20:58,090
who knows only the world of books.

1788
00:20:59,120 --> 00:21:05,190
I say all this, fully aware of how disrespectful I must sound,
but I do hope you will take my words to heart.

1789
00:21:06,310 --> 00:21:07,420
All right.

1790
00:21:16,630 --> 00:21:18,130
<i>Concerning the Maldura matter...</i>

1791
00:21:18,680 --> 00:21:22,510
<i>I got scathing criticism from
the more aggressive among the military. </i><i></i>

1792
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:24,760
I-I...

1793
00:21:25,790 --> 00:21:29,430
Elianna, I'll take charge of this matter from here.

1794
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:31,920
<i>I...</i>

1795
00:21:33,230 --> 00:21:41,780
<i>I was always protected by His Highness...
I truly am an big-headed bibliophile princess. </i><i></i>

1796
00:21:44,580 --> 00:21:48,540
<i>No, if I say it I'll miss him all the more...</i>

1797
00:21:50,900 --> 00:21:55,000
<i>Your Highness... Prince Christopher.</i>

1798
00:22:02,440 --> 00:22:06,170
Hey, are you Lady Elianna Bernstein?

